   "h": "The partner",
   "text": "The **Father McKenna Center** was opened in **1983** by St. Aloysius Parish in its church basement to honor **Fr. Horace McKenna, SJ** (1899–1982), Washington's priest to the poor. It is an independent 501(c)(3) in the Ignatian tradition. It serves men experiencing homelessness and poor neighbors through a **Day Program**, a **Hypothermia Program** (overnight in winter), a **Food Pantry** and a **Financial Stability Network**. It lists an **Immersion Service Learning Program**, which is how school groups come. — fathermckennacenter.org. ✅ In 2020 the hypothermia program sheltered about 10–20 men a season, and volunteers usually included Gonzaga students, school groups and college immersion groups. — Ignatian Solidarity Network, 2020. ⚠️ Six years old. In 2009 Street Sense reported more than 100 men a day using showers, laundry, meals and rest, and that several staff were formerly homeless themselves. ⚠️ 2009.",
