 "web": "These barriers land on the same person at once. Picture one man at the McKenna Center door. He grew up east of the river (2), and the apartment his family rented near North Capitol Street was torn down for towers (3). He came home from a federal prison hundreds of miles away with a record that a landlord's screening flags (5). He works some days, but rent needs a wage more than twice the minimum (1). He has no voting member in the Congress that reviews his city's budget (4). The people who do get meetings in that Congress are not usually him (6). Every door asks for an ID and an address he is still assembling (7). When he needs $400, the cheap lenders want a bank account and a credit history he does not have (8). No one barrier decided his life. Together they set the price.",
