   "plain": "D.C. caps most loan interest at **24% a year**, which ended storefront payday lending. Some online lenders partnered with out-of-state banks to charge far more, until D.C.'s Attorney General sued. Meanwhile 7% of D.C. households have no bank account at all, and a man with no account and no credit history cannot reach the cheap loans the cap protects.",
